# Flasher zips (microG installer, gapps, AnyKernel kernel zips, ...) need
# to run their installer scripts in recovery unrestricted: they toggle
# SELinux, mount block devices, create mountpoints, device nodes and
# symlinks, unpack cpio archives, and so on. LOS already makes the
# recovery domain permissive on userdebug/eng (device/lineage/sepolicy/
# common/private/recovery.te); mirror it here for the user variant, which
# is the variant zips are developed and tested against.
#
# The build guard refuses permissive domains in user policy
# (system/sepolicy/build/soong/policy.go, "permissive domains not allowed
# in user builds"); patches/system/sepolicy/0001-* adds the official
# module property permissive_domains_on_user_builds to sepolicy.recovery
# (the same mechanism microdroid uses for its "su" domain) so this one
# domain passes it.
#
# recovery_only() restricts this to the recovery variant of the policy:
# zero effect on the policy running in the system.
#
# "su" too: AnyKernel3 update-binaries run
#   echo "u:r:su:s0" > /proc/self/attr/current
# (osm0sis's workaround for loop-mounting apex payloads). On a permissive
# recovery that setcon now succeeds, and without a permissive su the shell
# lands in the tightly-restricted user-build su domain and dies mid-install
# (measured 23/11: update-binary exits 1 right on that line). userdebug
# recovery works precisely because it runs su permissive; mirror it.
recovery_only(`
permissive recovery;
permissive su;
')
